 ## Overview
-Fog Volume Grid Rendering is a technique for integrating `FogVolume` and `FogMaterial` nodes into a froxel-based volumetric fog system by adding their density, albedo, and emission properties to the froxels (volumetric grid cells) that the volume's shape covers [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of missing local fog contributions and negative density carving in real-time approximations, matching the behavior of Godot 4.6.3 [S1, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that focus on temporal stability or depth distribution, this method specifically handles the geometric mapping of arbitrary volume shapes (box, ellipsoid, cone, cylinder, world) and the texture-based density modulation required for static and dynamic fog volumes [S1, unofficial].
